<item>
  <title>Theatricality of Imperial Rome: Counterproductive Persecution of Free Speech</title>
  <link>https://camilosalgar.github.io/essays/essays/tacitus-theatricality-imperial-rome.html</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p><em>Directed Studies, Historical and Political Thought, Prof.&nbsp;Daniel Schillinger, Fall 2025</em></p>
<p>Traces through Tacitus’ Annals how Tiberius and Nero turned Roman politics into theater, and argues that persecuting free speech only raised its value.</p>
